commit b6f64bd09f51d7a803b75253be29d20d8a2a6941
Author: lora-dataset-studio <noreply@lora-dataset-studio.dev>
Date:   Tue Aug 25 23:51:04 2026 +0200

    feat(studio): a FLUX.2 Klein generation lane, and an honest refusal for the rest
    
    With his Klein LoRA finally reading as deployed (#52), lunchingfriar ticked it,
    hit Generate from the board, and got "no Z-Image model available" about a
    family he had never chosen (#53). The Test Studio had three generation lanes
    and every unrecognised family fell into the Z-Image one: first for its base
    models, then for its workflow.
    
    The deeper fault was mine, from the #52 fix: ONE list was answering TWO
    questions. FAMILIES says which families the studio can SEE, which the
    deployed-state lookup needs; it was also read as which families it can
    GENERATE with, so adding Klein to it offered Klein in a picker nothing could
    honour.
    
    - GENERATION_FAMILIES is now its own list, and available_families offers only
      what it can serve: a choice that fails on click is worse than no choice.
    - The three silent Z-Image fallbacks in this file are closed. A laneless family
      raises a refusal that NAMES the family asked for and says the LoRA itself is
      fine, instead of sending the user after a Z-Image model they never wanted.
    - FLUX.2 Klein gains a real lane: flux2_klein_t2i.json, an all-vanilla
      text-to-image graph (Klein is the edit engine everywhere else, so a test cell
      starting from a prompt needed a graph of its own), plus
      apply_klein_lora_test_settings. Engine assets come from the same resolvers as
      every other Klein path rather than the names frozen in the JSON, the tested
      LoRA and any user base go through whitelists, and cfg is pinned at 1.0
      because a swept CFG on a guidance-distilled model burns cells that then read
      as a bad checkpoint.
    - FLUX.1 and Anima get no lane, and this says why rather than pretending: the
      app holds no unet/vae/text-encoder setting for either, so there is nothing to
      generate with until they get an engine configuration. They now refuse
      honestly, which is the whole point of this change.
    
    Verified on GPU through the real code path: a Klein LoRA grid cell built by
    apply_klein_lora_test_settings rendered in 18s, with cfg 7.5 clamped to 1.0 and
    all three assets resolved from configuration. Tests pin the wiring, the
    whitelists, the clamp, and that every family offered for generation has a
    workflow file on disk.
    
    Reported by lunchingfriar (GitHub #53).
